#   2026-11-10f LOGIC_CASE_FLOAT_TEXT: CS2 passes a float output's value to a logic_case as text with a decimal place ('1.0'; CS:GO '1'), so whole-number cases fed by math_counter / math_remap / logic_compare outputs (and the logic_cases after them along OnDefault chains) become '1.0', and whole-number InValue parameters sent to those logic_cases get the same '.0'; links LOGIC_CASE_NUMERIC_FIX moved onto logic_compares are left as they were, the logic_cases it left (OnDefault outputs, text cases) are now covered. trigger_push.js: AIR_ACCEL_FIX, in the air CS2's acceleration of the push riding in the velocity is swapped for what CS:GO's AirAccelerate gave the own velocity (measured per player; sv_air_max_wishspeed / sv_airaccelerate from the Console API when the build has it)
#   2026-11-10e trigger_push from the in-game-tested tpush_test.js: CS2's own trigger_push pushes even at speed 0 (it uses 100), so TRIGGER_PUSH_SCRIPT now turns each trigger_push into a trigger_multiple (same brush, filter, outputs and flags; Once Only / Ladders taken off and kept in csgo_spawnflags; its push keys stay on it, csgo_class trigger_push marks it) instead of setting its speed to 0. trigger_push.js finds pushes by name: unnamed ones are named trigger_push__tp<N>, one sharing its name with another trigger_multiple is renamed <name>__tp<N> (outputs / template slots naming it also name the new one); point_templates spawning pushes (and their env_entity_makers) send RunScriptInput tpush_rescan. The script's pushing is tpush_test.js's (touches a tick late made up, the 3-unit lift with a kick CS2 doesn't pull back, brief touches, respawn reset, props by mass, grenades, Once Only, OnlyFallingPlayers, speed 0 = 100). The entity / IO reports compare a converted push as the trigger_push it was. TRIGGER_PUSH_SCRIPT False leaves CS2's trigger_push as it is (no more putting back an earlier run's speed)
