#   2026-11-08i water and overlays (ba_jail_os_gulag_d): a func_water's side and bottom faces with the water material become toolsnodraw (CS2 makes water of every water-material face, so water brushes with water on all sides made the whole map water; CS:GO drew only the top); the main map's water fades into the 3D skybox only when the skybox has water (otherwise Map UV Min / Max was the biggest pool's box and the other pools were not drawn); each static overlay's projection depth is cut to just past the faces CS:GO drew it on (its .vmf sides, an infodecal: the surface under it) where something lies behind them, as CS2 draws an overlay on every face within the depth (banners showed on the walls behind - STATIC_OVERLAY_FIT_DEPTH).
#   2026-11-08h Hammer crash on load (ba_jail_os_gulag_d): the sky player clip copy welded the sky faces' corners by position, so where separate sky brushes only touch at a corner one vertex was shared by separate fans of faces (one closed all round), which Hammer cannot open; the copy now keeps the sky mesh's own vertices (by_id) with a vertex per fan, which also clips doubled sky faces in one mesh (the 08g group copies are gone), and a rerun repairs a clip mesh an earlier run broke this way.
#   2026-11-08g weapon props: a prop keeps its class with CS2's weapon model (a Motion Disabled prop_physics became a prop_dynamic, which CS2 deletes - the weapon models have propdata - so the AWPs were missing; a rerun turns those back), and the weapons Valve renamed are found (w_rif_m4a1 is the M4A4: weapon_rif_m4a4; M4A1-S, USP-S, CZ75, Zeus, C4, defuser, grenades, healthshot and six knives too - WEAPON_PROP_RENAMES, from both games' items_game.txt). Sky player clip: the sky faces Valve's importer had merged into a func_water mesh (mg_hellz: 144, mostly ceilings; the water pass later puts them back into the world) get player clip too, and sky faces one mesh cannot hold (doubled faces sharing an edge: mg_n64_goldeneye, 279 left without clip) are copied as several clip meshes.
#   2026-11-08f lasers / teslas / spotlights as CS:GO drew them (Source SDK 2013 beam code, no tuned numbers): beams 2 x width, rendercolor x renderamt / 255, sprite every 100 units scrolling 100 x (TextureScroll / 10)^2 u/s, noise bend, start / end sparks, env_beam shade / taper flags and life / StrikeTime strikes (StrikeOnce), no particle for a laser with no target; an end that does not move apart from the start baked into the particle (no control point marker); spotlights get beam (glow_test02 x 64/255, constant width, fading over its traced length) and halo (light_glow03, 120 units, front only, Valve lamp-glow visibility); teslas trace CS:GO's sparks (2/3 around + 1/3 random, 3 retries, fractal noise x16, branches, 2 x thick -> 2, brightness 200, end glows) as one particle per tesla cycling its sparks on two alternating entities, colour copies sharing files through tint_cp / tint_cp_color (TESLA_TINT_CP); colours used as linear values as CS:GO did (m_bGammaCorrectVertexColors off). The old generated beam / glow textures, per-arc tesla entities and centre glow are gone, and a rerun folds older output into the new form. VTF reader: non-square textures were read from the wrong offset (every mip below the top one sized as if square: shifted sideways, frames missing; the tesla texture became two hollow edges).
#   2026-11-08e overlay quad materials on a map that already went through the script: <material>_quad.vmat is rebuilt from its ported base material (it was reported missing - no Source1 <name>_quad.vmt - and left missing when the addon did not have it).
#   2026-11-08d water drawn everywhere: the converted water materials set Map UV Min / Max over the whole world on maps without a 3D skybox (csgo_water_fancy discards water outside that box; the shader default ends at x / y 10241), and are compiled by the script after the water pass every run (Hammer kept an older compile: the 08b change never reached the game).
#   2026-11-08a brush entity copies: the importer's world copy of a brush entity with no origin key lies exactly on the entity (func_conveyors that never pushed, func_breakable_surf windows doubled by panes that do not break, func_water shells, doors) - removed face by face, never a real .vmf world brush (ENTITY_COPY_FIX).
#   2026-11-07m hairline cracks closed by default: both sides of a crack go onto the .vmf planes of the visible faces there (shortest move, positions only - no merged vertices, so no pinched corners); the importer's pulled corners (a floor corner dragged 0.18 down to a wall bottom) left slits to the void.
#   2026-11-07l review fixes: water pass crash (unbound old) and pool grouping, CS2_VERIFY_FOLDER None / empty, door outputs and lighting no longer rewrite an unchanged map (no-op saves skipped, backups made at write time), prefab files deleted only after their map is saved, face-restore weld 0.01, crack log after the geometry passes, missing-entity aliases for this script's own conversions, sky clip orphan copy; faster cross products / polygon clip / face-scale lookup, shared VPK cache.
#   2026-11-07k cleanup: removed the passes FACE_RESTORE replaced (glass seal, culled faces, displacement seal), switched-off workarounds (mesh weld, physbox gap, lit additive, moved levels), unused code and the clean-up of older versions' output.
#   2026-11-07j no hairline cracks.
#   2026-11-07i face scales: a face's normal from the whole polygon (a point added along an edge left its first three corners on a line: no match, and the material's import ratio broke its scale); rebuilt / split faces start at a real corner.
#   2026-11-07h a displacement brush cuts nothing (as vbsp): walls reach its bottom and the brush tops under it are rebuilt, closing the gaps where the spawn sand dips; no nodraw seals.
#   2026-11-07e rebuilt faces never leave a corner shared by faces that only touch there (bowtie)
SCRIPT_VERSION = "2026-11-24k laser noise across the beam only, ends pinned; exact physics hulls for physboxes; attribute filters use filterattribute"

_PASS_TIMES = []


def _timed(fn):
    """wrap a step so main() can report how long it took (PASS_TIMES)"""

    @functools.wraps(fn)
    def w(*a, **k):
        t0 = time.time()
        try:
            return fn(*a, **k)
        finally:
            _PASS_TIMES.append((fn.__name__, time.time() - t0))
    return w


_TIMED_STEPS = ("fix_tool_material_paths", "restore_missing_faces", "remove_origin_duplicates", "convert_display_brushes", "fix_mirrored_textures",
                "convert_soundscripts", "event_names_to_sounds", "sound_ranges", "write_soundevents", "import_model",
                "compile_models", "remap_bare_vmdl_materials", "fix_sound_entities", "check_sound_entities", "rename_plus_refs",
                "convert_fire_and_sparks", "convert_steam_and_trails", "fix_face_scales", "report_absurd_scale_faces", "static_overlay_report",
                "fix_static_overlays", "convert_entity_overlays", "rename_props_by_mass", "fix_trigger_materials", "fix_null_params",
                "check_player_equips", "fix_brush_render", "add_water_volumes", "add_map_scripts", "add_door_default_sounds", "add_button_sounds", "convert_soft_barriers", "convert_shared_teleports", "convert_equips", "collapse_prefabs", "split_3d_skybox", "rebuild_map_lighting", "report_entity_seams",
                "make_radars", "report_missing_entities", "report_dropped_io", "convert_one_vtf_to_vtex", "find_same_name_elsewhere",
                "_scan_vmaps", "_save_map", "_new_map", "_flush_vmaps", "match_vmfs",
                "restore_skybox_shell", "sync_skybox_lighting", "fix_mesh_links", "convert_addoutputs", "convert_lasers_and_teslas",
                "convert_particle_systems", "fix_named_illusionaries", "sky_occluder_and_clips", "fix_obsolete_entities",
                "port_skybox_materials", "add_door_unbreakable", "prepare_trigger_pushes", "weld_near_vertices", "seal_hairline_cracks", "split_long_physbox_pieces", "fix_skewed_texture_axes", "convert_spotlights", "fix_counter_cases",
                "fix_glass_backs", "fix_glass_flush", "fix_light_inputs", "fix_rotdoor_direction", "rebuild_displacements", "remove_entity_copies",
                "swap_weapon_props", "fix_cs2_keyvalues", "compile_generated_assets", "fit_overlay_depths")


def main():
    global RUN
    RUN = RunState()
    if PASS_TIMES:
        for _n in _TIMED_STEPS:
            if _n in globals() and callable(globals()[_n]) and not hasattr(globals()[_n], "__wrapped__"):
                globals()[_n] = _timed(globals()[_n])
    _t_start = time.time()
    print(f"Running: {os.path.abspath(__file__)}  (version {SCRIPT_VERSION})")
    _v = cs2_vpk()
    if USE_CS2_VPK:
        for _p, _c in _v.loaded:
            print(f"  CS2 VPK index: {os.path.relpath(_p, CS2_GAME_DIR)}  ({_c:,} files)")
        for _e in _v.errors:
            print(f"  [WARN] CS2 VPK not read: {_e}")
        if not _v.loaded:
            print(f"  [WARN] no CS2 *_dir.vpk found under {CS2_GAME_DIR}; using extracted folders only")
        else:
            for _top in ("particles/", "sounds/", "soundevents/", "materials/", "models/"):
                print(f"  CS2 reference {_top:<13} {sum(1 for _f in _v.files if _f.startswith(_top)):,} files in VPK")
    if CS2_VERIFY_FOLDER and os.path.isdir(CS2_VERIFY_FOLDER):
        print(f"  CS2 extracted folder in use as well: {CS2_VERIFY_FOLDER}")
    vmaps, primary = enumerate_vmaps(VMAP_PATH)
    if not vmaps:
        print("No VMAP files found to scan.")
        return
    vmap_root = Path(VMAP_PATH)
    export_dir = Path(EXPORT_DIR) if EXPORT_DIR is not None else derive_export_dir(primary if primary else vmap_root)
    RUN.addon_dir = export_dir
    log_prefix = primary.stem if primary else vmap_root.name if vmap_root.is_dir() else vmaps[0].stem

    def log(name):
        return os.path.join(LOG_DIR, f"{log_prefix}_{name}.txt")

    def write_log(name, lines):
        Path(log(name)).write_text("\n".join(lines), encoding="utf-8")

    def step(name, lines, head=None):
        """write a step's log lines to <prefix>_<name>.txt and print its summary: head, by default the first line without its '# '
        ("" = print nothing). -> lines"""
        write_log(name, lines)
        if head is None:
            head = lines[0][2:] if lines else ""
        if head:
            print(f"  {head}  (details: {Path(log(name)).name})")
        return lines

    def tail(lines, label):
        """'<label>: <what the first line says after its last ': '>' (the summary form most steps use)"""
        return f"{label}: " + (lines[0].split(": ")[-1] if lines else "none")

    def per_vmf(name, fn, maps, need_vmf=True, head=None, write_empty=True):
        """run fn(maps of one .vmf, that .vmf) for each .vmf (maps without one: skipped when need_vmf, else run with "") and log it as one
        step. With one .vmf (the usual case) this is just fn(maps, vmf); with several, each .vmf's part is marked in the log and printed.
        head(lines) -> the summary to print for one part. -> all lines"""
        groups = group_by_vmf(maps, vmf_of, need_vmf)
        lines, heads = [], []
        for vmf, group in groups:
            part = fn(group, vmf)
            if len(groups) > 1:
                lines.append(f"# ===== {', '.join(os.path.basename(str(v)) for v in group)}  (.vmf: {vmf or 'none'})")
            lines += part
            h = head(part) if head else (part[0][2:] if part else "")
            if h:
                heads.append(h + (f"  [{os.path.basename(vmf) if vmf else 'no .vmf'}]" if len(groups) > 1 else ""))
        if lines or write_empty:
            write_log(name, lines)
        for h in heads:
            for h_ in h.split("\n"):
                print(f"  {h_.strip()}  (details: {Path(log(name)).name})")
        return lines

    if COLLAPSE_PREFABS:
        _pf_log, _pf_moved = collapse_prefabs(vmaps, BACKUP_DIR)
        if any(x.startswith(("COLLAPSED", "KEPT", "ORPHAN")) for x in _pf_log):
            step("prefabs", _pf_log)
            vmaps = [v for v in vmaps if _npath(v) not in _pf_moved]
        vmaps = [v for v in vmaps if Path(v).is_file()]     # anything moved away under another spelling of its path
    RUN.overlay_vmats.update(static_overlay_materials(vmaps))
    if MATERIAL_BRACE_FIX:                       # an overlay whose material name has a stray '{': the material without it is the overlay's
        RUN.overlay_vmats |= {_brace_material(x).lower() for x in RUN.overlay_vmats if "{" in x}
    if MESH_LINK_FIX:
        step("mesh_links", fix_mesh_links(vmaps))
    if PHYSBOX_MESH_CLOSE:
        step("physbox_meshes", weld_near_vertices(vmaps, PHYSBOX_MESH_CLOSE, classes=PHYSBOX_MESH_CLASSES, require_closed=True, kind="physbox_close"))
    if PHYSBOX_SPLIT_LONG:
        step("physbox_split", split_long_physbox_pieces(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))

    # each map's own .vmf (by name); recomputed below once the 3D skybox maps exist
    vmf_of, _vmf_notes = match_vmfs(vmaps, primary)
    if SKYBOX_MATERIALS:
        # before the 3D skybox split: the skybox map's env_sky is copied from the main map's
        step("sky_material", port_skybox_materials(vmaps, vmf_of, export_dir))
    if SKYBOX_SPLIT:
        _sk_new = []

        def _split(group, vmf):
            lines, made = split_3d_skybox(group, vmf, BACKUP_DIR)
            _sk_new.extend(made)
            return lines
        per_vmf("skybox_split", _split, _main_vmaps(vmaps, primary), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if any(x.startswith(("SPLIT", "CHECK")) for x in ls) else "")
        vmaps = sorted(set(vmaps) | {Path(x) for x in _sk_new})
        vmf_of, _vmf_notes = match_vmfs(vmaps, primary)
        per_vmf("skybox_walls", restore_skybox_shell, [v for v in vmaps if v.name.lower().endswith("_skybox.vmap")], need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: "", write_empty=False)
        _skl = sync_skybox_lighting(_main_vmaps(vmaps, primary))
        if _skl:
            step("skybox_lighting", _skl, "")
        _skc = fix_skybox_cameras(_main_vmaps(vmaps, primary))
        step("skybox_camera", _skc, _skc[0][2:] if any(x.startswith(("CAMERA", "CHECK")) for x in _skc) else "")
    for _n in _vmf_notes:
        print("  " + _n)
    _vmf_groups = group_by_vmf(vmaps, vmf_of)
    for _vmf, _group in _vmf_groups:
        print(f"  reference .vmf: {_vmf}" + (f"  (for {', '.join(os.path.basename(str(v)) for v in _group)})" if len(_vmf_groups) > 1 or len(_group) < len(vmaps) else ""))
    _no_vmf = [v for v in vmaps if not vmf_of.get(v)]
    if _no_vmf:
        print("  [WARN] NO .vmf OF THE SAME NAME FOUND for " + ", ".join(os.path.basename(str(v)) for v in _no_vmf[:4]) + (" ..." if len(_no_vmf) > 4 else "")
              + ". Skipped for them: rebuilding the faces the import lost, origin-duplicate removal, water depth (flat water can't be swum in),"
              " missing-entity and dropped-IO reports.\n"
              f"         Looked for <map name>.vmf in: {', '.join(os.path.join(r, 'maps') for r in SOURCE1_ROOTS[:2])}, {os.path.join(SCRIPT_DIR, 'maps')} and next to the vmap."
              " Set SOURCE1_ROOT to this map's source folder, put the .vmf (named like the map) in one of those, or set STATIC_OVERLAY_VMF to its path.")

    # geometry repairs first, so materials they bring back (a restored floor) are converted by the asset scan below
    # (the .vmf passes skip 3D skybox maps, _playable_vmaps: the .vmf's geometry is the main map's, not theirs)
    if CONVEYOR_SCROLL:            # first: the .vmf passes and the asset scan see the conveyors' base material names
        _cr = conveyor_materials_revert(vmaps)
        if _cr:
            step("conveyor_revert", _cr, "")
    if TOOL_MATERIAL_PATH_FIX:
        _tp = fix_tool_material_paths(vmaps, export_dir)
        step("tool_material_paths", _tp, tail(_tp, "tool material paths"))
    if MATERIAL_BRACE_FIX:         # before the passes that match faces / overlays to the .vmf (they read its names through the same fix)
        step("brace_materials", fix_brace_materials(vmaps))
    if MISSING_BLACK_FIX:          # likewise, and before the asset scan (so the missing material is no longer asked for)
        _bm = fix_missing_black_materials(vmaps)
        step("black_materials", _bm, tail(_bm, "missing black materials"))
    if RENDER_TARGET_BLACK:        # the brush entity faces the import left out (a func_monitor's screen): back, black
        per_vmf("render_target_faces", restore_render_target_faces, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=True,
                head=lambda part: tail(part, "render-target screens") if part else "")
    if FACE_RESTORE:
        per_vmf("missing_faces", restore_missing_faces, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "missing faces"))
    if GLASS_BACK_FIX:
        per_vmf("glass_backs", fix_glass_backs, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "decompile nodraw"))
    if DROPPED_BRUSH_FIX:
        per_vmf("dropped_brushes", restore_dropped_brush_entities, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "dropped brush entities"))
    if ORIGIN_DUPLICATE_FIX:
        per_vmf("origin_duplicates", lambda g, v: remove_origin_duplicates(g, v, BACKUP_DIR), _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "origin duplicates"))
    if ENTITY_COPY_FIX:
        per_vmf("entity_copies", remove_entity_copies, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "entity copies"))
    if REPORT_DROPPED_IO and RESTORE_SELF_IO:
        # the outputs to !self / !activator / !caller the importer dropped go back BEFORE the passes that rebuild outputs (AddOutput, counters,
        # teleports ...): put back at the end, as they were, a fresh import left them all unconverted (harero: 114 AddOutputs) while a rerun
        # converted them. The report at the end still lists what is dropped (and puts back anything a later pass lost)
        per_vmf("dropped_io_restore", lambda g, v: [r for r in report_dropped_io(g, v, restore_self=True) if r.startswith(("RESTORED", "# ="))],
                _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: (f"dropped outputs to !self / !activator / !caller put back: {sum(1 for r in ls if r.startswith('RESTORED'))}"
                                                         if any(r.startswith("RESTORED") for r in ls) else ""))
    if ILLUSIONARY_IO_FIX:                       # before the display pass, so the func_illusionary it rebuilds become world in the same run
        per_vmf("named_illusionary", fix_named_illusionaries, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "func_illusionary"))
    if MAKER_TEMPLATE_AT_ENTITY:
        _mo = maker_template_at_entity(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("maker_offsets", _mo, _mo[0][2:] if _mo else "")
    if PHYSBOX_SIDE_GAP > 0:
        _pg = physbox_side_gaps(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("physbox_gaps", _pg, _pg[0][2:] if _pg else "")
    if DISPLAY_BRUSH_TO_WORLD:
        per_vmf("display_brushes", convert_display_brushes, vmaps, need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "display brushes"))
    if CRACK_FIX:       # after the passes that add world geometry (restored faces, display brushes), so the log shows the cracks this run
        per_vmf("cracks", seal_hairline_cracks, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False)   # leaves, not only those the importer made
    if GLASS_FLUSH_FIX:
        per_vmf("glass_flush", fix_glass_flush, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
    if SKY_OCCLUDER or SKY_PLAYERCLIP:
        step("sky", sky_occluder_and_clips(vmaps))
    if DOOR_DEFAULT_SOUNDS:
        per_vmf("door_sounds", add_door_default_sounds, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:].split(". ")[0])
    if BUTTON_SOUNDS:     # before the soundscript step, which ports the Buttons.sndN names it writes
        per_vmf("button_sounds", add_button_sounds, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:].split(". ")[0])

    all_matches, vmap_counts = set(), []
    for vp_str, extracted in _scan_vmaps(vmaps):
        all_matches.update(extracted)
        vmap_counts.append((vp_str, len(extracted)))
    _ovl = _screen_overlay_refs(vmaps)
    if _ovl:
        _ovl_hit = sorted(a for a in all_matches if normalize_candidate(a) in _ovl)
        all_matches.difference_update(_ovl_hit)
        write_log("screen_overlay_refs", ["# env_screenoverlay OverlayName* materials: not converted to .vmat and not listed as missing (the names are "
                                          "relative to materials/, not asset paths). SCREEN_OVERLAYS draws their textures as Panorama images instead."]
                  + [f"SKIPPED\t{a}" for a in _ovl_hit])

    write_log("vmaps_scanned", (str(v) for v in vmaps))
    write_log("vmap_asset_counts", (f"{c}\t{p}" for p, c in vmap_counts))
    write_log("raw_extracted_union", sorted(all_matches))

    dropped_by_root, filtered = [], []
    sprite_refs = {}
    sound_report = []
    generated_particles = []
    steam_built = {}      # particle name -> make_steam_particle result (built once per run)
    loop_event_names = set()
    sound_events = {}      # event name -> 'sounds/x.vsnd' (or (list of vsnds, volume)) for converted Source1 sounds
    if CONVERT_SOUNDSCRIPTS and COPY_SOUNDS:
        ss_lines = convert_soundscripts(export_dir, vmaps, sound_events, loop_event_names, sound_report)
        write_log("soundscripts", ss_lines)
    soundscape_events = set()       # soundscape loops: heard everywhere (their range is set after sound_ranges)
    if CONVERT_SOUNDSCAPES and COPY_SOUNDS:
        write_log("soundscapes", convert_soundscapes(export_dir, vmaps, sound_events, loop_event_names, sound_report, soundscape_events))
    for a in sorted(all_matches):
        a2 = normalize_candidate(a)
        if MISSING_BLACK_FIX and a2.endswith(".vmat"):
            # MISSING_BLACK_FIX took the missing black material out of the map, but its name stays in the file's string table until Hammer
            # saves the map: asking for it means asking for CS2's black material
            a2 = normalize_candidate(_black_material(a2))
        if a2.endswith(".spr"):
            # Source1 sprites ("sprites/glow01.spr") are really materials/sprites/glow01.vmt
            body = a2[len("materials/"):] if a2.startswith("materials/") else a2
            mat = normalize_candidate("materials/" + body[:-4] + ".vmat")
            sprite_refs[a2] = mat
            a2 = mat
        (filtered if passes_root_filter(a2) else dropped_by_root).append(a2)
    write_log("dropped_by_rootfilter", sorted(set(dropped_by_root)))

    valid_assets, invalid_assets = [], []
    for asset in filtered:
        (valid_assets if is_valid_asset_path(asset) else invalid_assets).append(asset)

    processed, copied, converted = set(), set(), set()
    failed, models_todo, unsupported = [], set(), set()
    models_imported, models_skipped, orphan_records = set(), set(), set()
    iris_recs, iris_rows = set(), []               # EYE_IRIS_BAKE: .vmdl remaps to the baked eye materials, log lines
    status = {}                       # asset -> why it ended up without an output

    mdl_skip = () if MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM else tuple(x.lower() for x in MDL_SKIP_PREFIXES)      # MDL_SKIP_PREFIXES, lower case once
    mdl_trim_dir = Path(BACKUP_DIR) / "mdl_trim"                 # MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM: the stand-in Source1 folders
    _mdl_seqs = []

    def mdl_wanted(mdl_rel):
        """the sequences the maps play on a model (vmf_model_sequences, read once)"""
        if not _mdl_seqs:
            _mdl_seqs.append(vmf_model_sequences(vmf_of.values()))
        return _mdl_seqs[0].get(mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower(), set())
    import_enabled = IMPORT_MODELS
    if IMPORT_MODELS and not Path(CS_MDL_IMPORT_EXE).exists():
        print(f"[WARN] cs_mdl_import.exe not found ({CS_MDL_IMPORT_EXE}); models will only be listed.")
        import_enabled = False
    mdl_list_path = Path(log("mdl_single_import"))
    mdl_stdout_log = Path(log("cs_mdl_import_stdout"))
    mdl_fail_mem = _mdl_failures_load() if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES else {}     # earlier runs' failed model imports
    mdl_own_root = {}                                # model -> the Source1 folder its batch import used (MDL_CRASH_OTHER_SOURCE)
    mdl_keys, models_source_note = {}, {}            # model -> (failure key, files); model -> the other Source1 folder it was imported from

    def mdl_result(mkey, stamp, ok, msg):
        """MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES: remember a failed import (for these exact files), forget one that worked"""
        if not MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES:
            return
        if ok:
            mdl_fail_mem.pop(mkey, None)
        else:
            mdl_fail_mem[mkey] = (stamp, " ".join(str(msg).split())[:300])
    requested_all, verified_only = set(), set()
    already_in_cs2, vtex_converted = set(), set()       # for the summary: assets CS2 ships / .vtf converted to .vtex

    queue = deque(valid_assets)
    enqueued = set(valid_assets)

    referrers = {}                    # asset -> a few of the things that asked for it (for the missing_reasons log)
    cur_asset = [""]

    def note_referrer(dep: str, via: str):
        r = referrers.setdefault(dep, [])
        if via and via not in r and len(r) < 4:
            r.append(via)
    for _a in valid_assets:
        note_referrer(_a, "the map (.vmap)")

    def enqueue(dep: str):
        dep = normalize_candidate(dep)
        if dep and passes_root_filter(dep):
            note_referrer(dep, cur_asset[0])
        if dep and passes_root_filter(dep) and not dep.endswith("meshinfo.txt") \
                and dep not in processed and dep not in enqueued:
            queue.append(dep)
            enqueued.add(dep)

    def exists_out(rel: str) -> bool:
        return (export_dir / rel).exists()

    quad_materials_later = []         # <material>_quad.vmat the map references (rebuilt from <material>.vmat after the scan)

    def drain_queue():
        while queue:
            asset = normalize_candidate(queue.popleft())
            if asset in processed:
                continue
            cur_asset[0] = asset
            processed.add(asset)
            requested_all.add(asset)
            kind, found, _extra = find_asset(asset)
            if not kind and asset.endswith("_quad.vmat"):
                # this script's own overlay quad material (convert_entity_overlays: <material>_quad.vmat, made from the overlay's
                # material), referenced by a map that already went through the script; there is no Source1 <name>_quad.vmt, so it was
                # reported missing and, when the addon no longer had it, the quads showed the missing material. The base material is
                # ported like any other and the quad material rebuilt from it after the scan (quad_materials_later)
                quad_materials_later.append(asset)
                enqueue(asset[:-len("_quad.vmat")] + ".vmat")
                continue
            if not kind:
                if asset.endswith(".vpcf"):
                    _stem = os.path.splitext(os.path.basename(asset))[0]
                    _skv = parse_steam_particle_name(_stem) if (GENERATE_STEAM_PARTICLES and asset.startswith("particles/steam/")) else None
                    if _skv is not None:
                        if _stem not in steam_built:
                            steam_built[_stem] = make_steam_particle(export_dir, _stem, _skv)
                            generated_particles.extend(steam_built[_stem][2] if steam_built[_stem][0]
                                                       else [f"{_stem}\t{_steam_status(steam_built[_stem][1])}"])
                        if steam_built[_stem][0]:
                            copied.add(asset)
                        else:
                            status[asset] = steam_built[_stem][1]
                        continue
                    if asset.startswith(("particles/spritetrail/", "particles/spark/")):     # written (and rewritten every run) by the steam / trail / spark passes
                        copied.add(asset)
                        continue
                    ok_p, msg_p = (make_sprite_particle(export_dir, asset) if GENERATE_SPRITE_PARTICLES
                                   else (False, "sprite particle generation disabled"))
                    if ok_p:
                        generated_particles.append(f"{asset}\t{msg_p}")
                        copied.add(asset)
                        continue
                    status[asset] = ("particle system not in CS2; Source1 .pcf particles cannot be converted "
                                     f"({msg_p}); replace with a CS2 particle in Hammer")
                elif asset.endswith(".vsnd"):
                    status[asset] = "not in CS2 and no matching sound/*.wav|mp3 found in any Source1 root"
                else:
                    status[asset] = "not in CS2 and no Source1 source found in any root"
                continue

            if kind == "cs2_verify":
                verified_only.add(asset)
                already_in_cs2.add(asset)
                if asset.endswith(".vsnd") and WRITE_SOUNDEVENTS:
                    # CS2 has the file but an entity plays soundevents only (ambient_generic message = a path is silent): one event for it,
                    # named like the path, playing CS2's own file (nothing copied). mg_hellz mg6_sound / mg8_lunch: flashbang_explode1 / 2
                    _r = os.path.splitext(asset)[0]
                    _r = _r[len("sounds/"):] if _r.startswith("sounds/") else _r
                    sound_events.setdefault(SOUNDEVENT_PREFIX + _r.replace("/", "."), asset)
                if asset.endswith(".vmdl") and USE_CS2_VPK:
                    for _bm in cs2_vmdl_bad_materials(asset):
                        RUN.stub_cs2_vmats.add(f"{_bm}  (used by the CS2 model {asset}, missing or broken in CS2: ported from Source1 if a .vmt exists)")
                        enqueue(_bm)

            elif kind == "source1_vmt":
                vmat_rel = (os.path.splitext(asset)[0] + ".vmat").replace("+", "_")
                if exists_out(vmat_rel) and not OVERWRITE_EXISTING_VMATS:
                    ok, info = True, "kept existing"
                else:
                    ok, info = convert_one_vmt(export_dir, found, vmat_rel)
                if ok:
                    converted.add(vmat_rel)
                    for d in parse_vmat_dependencies(str(export_dir / vmat_rel)):
                        enqueue(d)
                elif info.startswith("UNSUPPORTED_SHADER:"):
                    shader_name = info.split(' :: ')[0].split(':', 1)[1]
                    unsupported.add(f"{asset}\t{shader_name}")
                    status[asset] = (f"Source1 water (shader {shader_name}): CS2 has no such material and none is picked for you; give the water a CS2 water material in Hammer"
                                     if shader_name.lower() == "water" else
                                     f"unsupported shader ({shader_name}): CS2 has no Refract (screen-warp / distortion) shader, so no vmat written. As an env_screenoverlay "
                                     "material it is obsolete with that entity (see the obsolete_entities log)" if shader_name.lower() == "refract" else
                                     f"unsupported shader ({shader_name}); no vmat written")
                else:
                    failed.append(f"{asset} :: {info}")
                    status[asset] = f"VMT found but conversion failed: {info}"

            elif kind == "source1_vtex":
                ok, info = convert_one_vtf_to_vtex(export_dir, found, asset)
                if ok:
                    vtex_converted.add(asset)
                else:
                    failed.append(f"{asset} :: {info}")

            elif kind == "source1_vtf":
                verified_only.add(asset)

            elif kind == "source1_raw":
                if copy_asset_to_export(export_dir, found, asset):
                    copied.add(asset)

            elif kind == "source1_sound":
                if COPY_SOUNDS:
                    dest_rel = asset
                    if asset.endswith(".vsnd"):
                        rest = os.path.splitext(asset)[0]
                        rest = rest[len("sounds/"):] if rest.startswith("sounds/") else rest
                        dest_rel = "sounds/" + rest + os.path.splitext(found)[1].lower()
                        event = SOUNDEVENT_PREFIX + rest.replace("/", ".")
                        sound_events[event] = asset
                        if is_looping_sound(found):
                            loop_event_names.add(event)
                    dest_rel, new_copy = place_sound(export_dir, found, dest_rel, sound_report)
                    if new_copy:
                        copied.add(asset if dest_rel == asset else f"{asset}\t<- {dest_rel}")
                    if dest_rel != asset and exists_out(dest_rel):
                        verified_only.add(asset)       # '<x>.vsnd' is satisfied by the copied '<x>.wav|mp3'
                else:
                    verified_only.add(asset)

            elif kind == "source1_model":
                mdl_rel = os.path.splitext(asset)[0] + ".mdl"
                imported = False
                mdl_mats = parse_mdl_materials(found)         # materials/<cdmaterials>/<name>.vmat from the .mdl
                if import_enabled:
                    if exists_out(asset) and not OVERWRITE_EXISTING_MODELS and not (MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM and mdl_trim_stale(mdl_trim_dir, mdl_rel, mdl_wanted(mdl_rel))):
                        imported = True                       # already in the addon folder (and with every sequence the map plays on it)
                    else:
                        skipped = bool(mdl_skip) and mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower().startswith(mdl_skip)
                        problems = mdl_sidecar_problems(Path(_extra), mdl_rel) if (PRECHECK_SIDECARS and not skipped) else []
                        sums = _mdl_checksum_problems(Path(_extra), mdl_rel) if (PRECHECK_SIDECARS and not skipped and not problems) else []
                        if (problems or sums) and not skipped:
                            # the map's own copy cannot be imported (a .vtx packed from another version of the model crashes the importer):
                            # the same model from another Source1 folder (the stock game's) when one has a complete, matching copy
                            alt = _mdl_other_source(mdl_rel, _extra)
                            if alt:
                                why_ = ("missing " + ", ".join(problems)) if problems else "; ".join(sums)
                                models_source_note[asset] = f"from {alt} (the copy in {_extra}: {why_})"
                                _extra, found = alt, str(_mdl_path(Path(alt), mdl_rel))
                                mdl_mats = parse_mdl_materials(found)
                                problems, sums = [], []
                        mkey = (mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower(), str(_extra).lower())
                        stamp = _mdl_stamp(Path(_extra), mdl_rel) if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and not skipped else ""
                        if sums and not problems:
                            models_skipped.add(f"{asset}\t{'; '.join(sums)}: cs_mdl_import stops with 'Invalid VTX file checksum' and crashes, so it is not run "
                                               f"(no other Source1 folder has a matching copy)\t<- {found}")
                            failed.append(f"{asset} :: model import failed :: {'; '.join(sums)} (not run)")
                            model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, False)
                            continue
                        if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and MDL_CRASH_OTHER_SOURCE and not skipped and not problems and mdl_fail_mem.get(mkey, ("",))[0] == stamp:
                            alt = _mdl_other_source(mdl_rel, _extra)
                            if alt:                  # the map's copy failed on an earlier run: the other folder's copy instead
                                models_source_note[asset] = (f"from {alt} (the copy in {_extra} failed to import on an earlier run: "
                                                             f"{mdl_fail_mem[mkey][1][:120]})")
                                _extra, found = alt, str(_mdl_path(Path(alt), mdl_rel))
                                mdl_mats = parse_mdl_materials(found)
                                mkey = (mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower(), str(_extra).lower())
                                stamp = _mdl_stamp(Path(_extra), mdl_rel)
                        if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and not skipped and not problems and mdl_fail_mem.get(mkey, ("",))[0] == stamp:
                            r_ni = mdl_try_no_includes(asset, _extra, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, f"on an earlier run: {mdl_fail_mem[mkey][1]}")
                            if r_ni and r_ni[0]:
                                models_imported.add(f"{asset}\t{r_ni[1]}\t{models_source_note[asset]}")
                                model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, True)
                                continue
                            failed.append(f"{asset} :: model import failed :: on an earlier run ({mdl_fail_mem[mkey][1]}); not tried again while its files "
                                          f"are unchanged (MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES) - delete its line in {_mdl_failures_path()} to try again"
                                          + (f" ({r_ni[1]})" if r_ni else ""))
                            model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, False)
                            continue
                        if skipped:
                            models_skipped.add(f"{asset}\tplayer / hostage model: not imported (MDL_SKIP_PREFIXES) - its animation set takes minutes to convert and it would "
                                               f"still be a plain prop; swap the prop for a stock CS2 character model or rebuild it as an agent\t<- {found}")
                            verified_only.add(asset)
                        elif problems:
                            models_skipped.add(f"{asset}\tmissing {', '.join(problems)}\t<- {found}")
                        elif MDL_BATCH:
                            pending_models.append((asset, found, mdl_import_root(asset, _extra, mdl_rel, mdl_mats), mdl_rel, mdl_mats))     # imported together after the queue drains
                            mdl_keys[mdl_rel] = (mkey, stamp)
                            mdl_own_root[mdl_rel] = _extra
                            for vmat in mdl_mats:
                                if find_in_source1(os.path.splitext(vmat)[0] + ".vmt")[0]:
                                    enqueue(vmat)
                            continue
                        else:
                            ok, msg = import_model(Path(mdl_import_root(asset, _extra, mdl_rel, mdl_mats)), mdl_rel, export_dir, mdl_list_path, mdl_stdout_log)
                            mdl_result(mkey, stamp, ok, msg)
                            if not ok:
                                r_ni = mdl_try_no_includes(asset, _extra, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, msg)
                                if r_ni:
                                    ok, msg = r_ni
                            if ok:
                                imported = True
                                models_imported.add(f"{asset}\t{msg}" + (f"\t{models_source_note[asset]}" if asset in models_source_note else ""))
                            else:
                                failed.append(f"{asset} :: model import failed :: {msg}")
                else:
                    imported = exists_out(asset)              # importer off: a model already in the addon is fine
                model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, imported)

    def mdl_try_no_includes(asset, root, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, why):
        """MDL_CRASH_NO_INCLUDES: the model from root imported once more with no shared animation files (remembered like any import).
        -> (ok, msg), or None when it has no shared files / the setting is off / this also failed on an earlier run"""
        if not MDL_CRASH_NO_INCLUDES or not root:
            return None
        try:
            nr, incs = mdl_noinclude_source(Path(root), mdl_rel, mdl_mats, mdl_trim_dir)
        except Exception as ex:                      # a file that cannot be read / written
            return False, f"{why}; MDL_CRASH_NO_INCLUDES could not make its copy ({ex})"
        if nr is None:
            return None
        n_key = (mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower(), str(root).lower() + "|no_includes")
        n_stamp = _mdl_stamp(Path(root), mdl_rel) if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES else ""
        if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and mdl_fail_mem.get(n_key, ("",))[0] == n_stamp:
            return False, f"{why}; without its shared files ({', '.join(incs)}) it failed on an earlier run too ({mdl_fail_mem[n_key][1][:120]})"
        if MDL_VTX_ONE_STRIP_GROUP:
            try:
                _same, vnote = mdl_vtx_fixed_source(Path(root), mdl_rel, mdl_mats, mdl_trim_dir, nr)   # fixes the .vtx inside nr itself
            except Exception as ex:
                vnote = f"MDL_VTX_ONE_STRIP_GROUP failed ({ex}); imported with its own .vtx"
            if vnote and vnote not in models_source_note.get(asset, ""):
                models_source_note[asset] = (models_source_note[asset] + "; " if asset in models_source_note else "") + vnote
        print(f"  models: {mdl_rel} failed with its shared animation files; importing it without them...", flush=True)
        ok_, msg_ = import_model(Path(nr), mdl_rel, export_dir, mdl_list_path, mdl_stdout_log)
        mdl_result(n_key, n_stamp, ok_, msg_)
        if not ok_:
            return False, f"{why}; without its shared files ({', '.join(incs)}) it failed too: {msg_}"
        lost = sorted(w for w in mdl_wanted(mdl_rel) if not w.startswith("@"))
        own = {s_["name"].lower() for s_ in ((mdl_read(Path(_mdl_path(Path(root), mdl_rel)).read_bytes()) or {}).get("seqs") or [])}
        lost = [w for w in lost if w.lower() not in own]
        models_source_note[asset] = ((models_source_note[asset] + "; ") if asset in models_source_note else "") + (
            f"MDL_CRASH_NO_INCLUDES: imported WITHOUT its shared animation files ({', '.join(incs)}), only its own sequences "
            f"(with them cs_mdl_import failed: {' '.join(str(why).split())[:120]})"
            + (f"; MISSING sequences the map plays on it: {', '.join(lost)} (it shows its own default pose)" if lost else ""))
        return True, msg_

    def mdl_import_root(asset, root, mdl_rel, mdl_mats):
        """the folder cs_mdl_import reads a model from: its Source1 folder, or with MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM the stand-in holding its trimmed copy"""
        tr = None
        if MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM:
            try:
                tr, note = mdl_trimmed_source(Path(root), mdl_rel, mdl_wanted(mdl_rel), mdl_mats, mdl_trim_dir)
            except Exception as ex:                      # a file that cannot be read / written: imported whole, as before
                tr, note = None, f"MDL_INCLUDE_TRIM failed ({ex}); imported with its whole animation set"
            if note:
                models_source_note[asset] = (models_source_note[asset] + "; " if asset in models_source_note else "") + note
        if MDL_VTX_ONE_STRIP_GROUP:
            try:
                tr, note = mdl_vtx_fixed_source(Path(root), mdl_rel, mdl_mats, mdl_trim_dir, tr)
            except Exception as ex:                      # imported from its own .vtx, as before
                note = f"MDL_VTX_ONE_STRIP_GROUP failed ({ex}); imported with its own .vtx"
            if note and note not in models_source_note.get(asset, ""):
                models_source_note[asset] = (models_source_note[asset] + "; " if asset in models_source_note else "") + note
        return str(tr) if tr is not None else root

    def model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, imported):
        cur_asset[0] = asset
        if imported:
            # dependencies of what the importer produced (materials, refs, ...)
            vmdl_out, refs_out = mdl_output_footprint(export_dir, mdl_rel)
            if vmdl_out.is_file():
                for d in parse_vmdl_dependencies(str(vmdl_out)):
                    enqueue(d)
            if refs_out.is_dir():
                for fp in refs_out.rglob("*.dmx"):
                    rooted, orphans = parse_dmx_deps_nul(str(fp))
                    # MISSING_BLACK_FIX: a material named black that exists nowhere is not asked for; the .vmdl gets a remap to CS2's black
                    blk_rooted, blk_bare, blk_recs = model_black_remaps(str(fp), rooted, orphans, asset, mdl_mats)
                    orphan_records.update(blk_recs)
                    for d in rooted:
                        enqueue(blk_rooted.get(d, d))
                    for o in orphans:
                        if o in blk_bare:
                            enqueue(blk_bare[o])
                            orphan_records.add((o, asset, (blk_bare[o],)))
                            continue
                        # bare name in the DMX: find its folder via the .mdl material list,
                        # else guess materials/<model folder>/<name>
                        cands = [p for p in mdl_mats if p.rsplit("/", 1)[-1] == o.lower()]
                        if not cands:
                            guess = normalize_candidate("materials/" + asset.rsplit("/", 1)[0] + "/" + o)
                            if find_in_source1(os.path.splitext(guess)[0] + ".vmt")[0]:
                                cands = [guess]
                                enqueue(guess)
                        orphan_records.add((o, asset, tuple(cands)))
            if EYE_IRIS_BAKE and refs_out.is_dir():
                dnames = {}
                for fp in refs_out.rglob("*.dmx"):
                    dnames.update(_dmx_material_names(str(fp)))
                try:
                    recs_, rows_ = bake_model_irises(export_dir, asset, found, dnames)
                except Exception as ex:
                    recs_, rows_ = [], [f"FAILED\t{asset}\t{type(ex).__name__}: {ex}"]
                iris_recs.update(recs_)
                iris_rows.extend(rows_)
        else:
            models_todo.add(f"{asset}\t<- {found}")
            verified_only.add(asset)     # reported in the models log, not as missing
        # materials named in the Source1 .mdl itself
        for vmat in mdl_mats:
            if find_in_source1(os.path.splitext(vmat)[0] + ".vmt")[0]:
                enqueue(vmat)

    def drain_all():
        drain_queue()
        while pending_models:                    # MDL_BATCH: the models found so far, one importer run per Source1 folder
            batch = pending_models[:]
            pending_models.clear()
            by_root = {}
            for it in batch:
                by_root.setdefault(it[2], []).append(it)
            for root, items in by_root.items():
                print(f"  models: importing {len(items)} model(s) in one cs_mdl_import run...", flush=True)
                left, res, stuck = list(items), {}, False
                while left:
                    r_ = import_models_batch(Path(root), [it[3] for it in left], export_dir, mdl_list_path, mdl_stdout_log)
                    res.update(r_)
                    bad = [it for it in left if not r_.get(it[3], (False, ""))[0]]
                    # the importer converts the list in order; when it crashes on a model, none after it are converted. If that is what
                    # happened (everything from the first unconverted model on is unconverted), the one it stopped at goes on its own below
                    # and the rest in another batch run instead of one importer run each
                    if len(bad) <= 2 or bad != left[len(left) - len(bad):]:
                        break
                    if len(bad) == len(left):
                        if stuck:
                            break                # two runs in a row made nothing: one at a time below
                        stuck = True
                    else:
                        stuck = False
                    print(f"  models: the importer stopped at {bad[0][3]}; {len(bad) - 1} model(s) after it in another run...", flush=True)
                    left = bad[1:]
                for asset, found, _x, mdl_rel, mdl_mats in items:
                    ok, msg = res.get(mdl_rel, (False, "not run"))
                    if not ok:                   # not produced by the batch: one at a time, with retries
                        ok, msg = import_model(Path(root), mdl_rel, export_dir, mdl_list_path, mdl_stdout_log)
                    if mdl_rel in mdl_keys:
                        mdl_result(mdl_keys[mdl_rel][0], mdl_keys[mdl_rel][1], ok, msg)
                    own = mdl_own_root.get(mdl_rel)
                    alt = _mdl_other_source(mdl_rel, own) if (not ok and MDL_CRASH_OTHER_SOURCE and own) else None
                    if alt:                      # the map's copy failed: the same model from another Source1 folder
                        print(f"  models: {mdl_rel} failed from {own}; importing the copy in {alt}...", flush=True)
                        a_found = str(_mdl_path(Path(alt), mdl_rel))
                        a_mats = parse_mdl_materials(a_found)
                        a_key = (mdl_rel.replace("\\", "/").lower(), str(alt).lower())
                        a_stamp = _mdl_stamp(Path(alt), mdl_rel) if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES else ""
                        if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and mdl_fail_mem.get(a_key, ("",))[0] == a_stamp:
                            msg = f"{msg}; the copy in {alt} failed on an earlier run too ({mdl_fail_mem[a_key][1][:120]})"
                        else:
                            ok2, msg2 = import_model(Path(mdl_import_root(asset, alt, mdl_rel, a_mats)), mdl_rel, export_dir, mdl_list_path, mdl_stdout_log)
                            mdl_result(a_key, a_stamp, ok2, msg2)
                            if ok2:
                                models_source_note[asset] = (f"from {alt} (the copy in {own} failed to import: {' '.join(str(msg).split())[:120]})"
                                                             + (f"; {models_source_note[asset]}" if asset in models_source_note else ""))
                                ok, msg = True, msg2
                                found, mdl_mats = a_found, a_mats
                            else:
                                msg = f"{msg}; the copy in {alt} failed too: {msg2}"
                    if not ok:                   # still failing: once more without its shared animation files
                        r_ni = mdl_try_no_includes(asset, alt or own or root, mdl_rel, a_mats if alt else mdl_mats, msg)
                        if r_ni:
                            ok, msg = r_ni
                            if ok and alt:
                                found, mdl_mats = a_found, a_mats
                    if ok:
                        models_imported.add(f"{asset}\t{msg}" + (f"\t{models_source_note[asset]}" if asset in models_source_note else ""))
                    else:
                        failed.append(f"{asset} :: model import failed :: {msg}")
                    model_done(asset, found, mdl_rel, mdl_mats, ok)
            drain_queue()

    pending_models = []
    drain_all()
    if ENABLE_STRATEGY_B_MODEL_SCAN:
        cur_asset[0] = "scan of the models already in the addon folder"
        for d in scan_addon_models_for_deps(export_dir):
            enqueue(d)
        drain_all()
    for q in sorted(set(quad_materials_later)):
        base_ = q[:-len("_quad.vmat")] + ".vmat"
        try:
            r_ = _build_quad_material(base_, Path(export_dir))
        except Exception as ex:
            r_ = f"could not be built ({type(ex).__name__}: {ex})"
        if isinstance(r_, tuple):
            copied.add(q)
        else:
            status[q] = f"overlay quad material (this script makes it from {base_}): {r_}"

    def exists_hashed_color_vtex(folder_rel: str, base: str) -> bool:
        d = export_dir / folder_rel
        if not d.is_dir():
            return False
        base_low = base.lower()
        try:
            return any(f.lower().startswith(base_low + "_color_tga_") and f.lower().endswith((".vtex", ".vtex_c"))
                       for f in os.listdir(d))
        except Exception:
            return False

    def source1_request_satisfied(req: str) -> bool:
        low = req.lower()
        if low.endswith(".vmt") and low.startswith("materials/"):
            return exists_out(os.path.splitext(req)[0] + ".vmat")
        if low.endswith(".vsnd"):
            base_no_ext = os.path.splitext(req)[0]
            return exists_out(base_no_ext + ".wav") or exists_out(base_no_ext + ".mp3")
        if low.endswith(".vtf") and low.startswith("materials/"):
            base_no_ext = os.path.splitext(req)[0]
            cands = [base_no_ext + s for s in (".vtex", ".vtex_c", "_color.vtex", "_color.vtex_c", "_color.tga", "_color.png")]
            return any(exists_out(c) for c in cands) or \
                exists_hashed_color_vtex(os.path.dirname(base_no_ext), os.path.basename(base_no_ext))
        return False

    missing_final = set()
    _water_later = {u.split("\t")[0] for u in unsupported if u.split("\t")[-1].lower() == "water"} if (WATER_VOLUMES and WATER_CONVERT) else set()
    for a in sorted(requested_all):
        if a in verified_only or exists_out(a) or source1_request_satisfied(a) or a in _water_later:
            continue
        missing_final.add(a)
    for t in RUN.missing_textures:
        if not source1_request_satisfied(t):
            missing_final.add(t)

    write_log("processed", sorted(processed))
    write_log("missing", sorted(missing_final))
    write_log("copied", sorted(copied))
    write_log("converted_vmats", sorted(converted))
    write_log("failed", failed)
    if MDL_REMEMBER_FAILURES and import_enabled:
        _mdl_failures_save(mdl_fail_mem)
    write_log("models_to_convert", sorted(models_todo))
    write_log("unsupported_shaders", sorted(unsupported))
    reasons = []
    same_name = {}
    if MISSING_SUGGESTIONS and missing_final:
        same_name = find_same_name_elsewhere(missing_final)
    kinds = {}
    for a in sorted(missing_final):
        users = sorted(RUN.missing_texture_users.get(a, ()))
        if status.get(a):
            why = status[a]
        elif a in RUN.missing_textures:
            why = "texture not found in any Source1 root or in CS2" + (f" (needed by {', '.join(users[:3])}{' ...' if len(users) > 3 else ''})" if users else "")
        else:
            why = "referenced, but no output was produced (the converter did not report why; see the failed / unsupported logs)"
        extra = []
        if referrers.get(a):
            extra.append("referenced by: " + "; ".join(referrers[a]))
        if same_name.get(a):
            extra.append("same name exists elsewhere: " + "; ".join(same_name[a]))
        reasons.append("\t".join([a, why] + extra))
        ext = os.path.splitext(a)[1].lstrip(".") or "?"
        kinds[ext] = kinds.get(ext, 0) + 1
    if kinds:
        print("  missing assets: " + ", ".join(f"{n} .{k}" for k, n in sorted(kinds.items(), key=lambda t: -t[1])) +
              f" (reasons, who referenced them and same-name files elsewhere: {log('missing_reasons')})")
    write_log("missing_reasons", reasons)
    rederived = event_names_to_sounds(export_dir, vmaps, sound_events, loop_event_names, sound_report) \
        if REDERIVE_EVENTS_FROM_NAMES else []
    kept_events = []
    if KEEP_PREVIOUS_SOUNDEVENTS:
        # entities renamed to the event name no longer contain the .vsnd path, so the harvest does not see the
        # sound again; keep what an earlier run generated instead of dropping it from the file
        for _n, (_files, _vol, _had_base) in read_generated_events(export_dir).items():
            if _n not in sound_events:
                sound_events[_n] = (_files, _vol)
                kept_events.append(_n)
                if _had_base:
                    loop_event_names.add(_n)
    Path(log("soundevent_map")).write_text(
        "\n".join(sorted(f"{', '.join(v[0] if isinstance(v, tuple) else [v])}\t-> {k}"
                         + ("\t(kept from an earlier run; no longer found in the vmap)" if k in kept_events else "")
                         for k, v in sound_events.items())),
        encoding="utf-8")
    if rederived:
        write_log("soundevents_rederived", (f"{n}\t{why}" for n, why in rederived))
    write_log("sound_report", sorted(sound_report))
    if WRITE_SOUNDEVENTS and sound_events:
        _vols = {} if SOUND_ENTITY_VOLUME else None
        _levels = {}
        _ranges = sound_ranges(vmaps, sound_events, _vols, _levels) if (SOUND_RANGE_CURVES or SOUND_ENTITY_VOLUME) else {}
        if SOUND_RANGE_CURVES:
            for _n in soundscape_events:
                _ranges[_n] = SOUND_EVERYWHERE_RADIUS     # a soundscape loop has no place: heard alike everywhere in it
        else:
            _ranges = {}
        if _vols:
            _vols = {n: v for n, v in _vols.items() if n not in kept_events and v != 1.0}      # events kept from an earlier run already carry their volume
            if _vols:
                Path(log("soundevent_entity_volume")).write_text(
                    "# ambient_generic Volume (health/10) multiplied into the event volume\n" + "\n".join(f"{n}\t{v:g}" for n, v in sorted(_vols.items())),
                    encoding="utf-8")
        if _ranges:
            Path(log("soundevent_ranges")).write_text(
                "\n".join(f"{n}\t{'everywhere' if r >= SOUND_EVERYWHERE_RADIUS else int(r)}" for n, r in sorted(_ranges.items())),
                encoding="utf-8")
        write_soundevents(export_dir, sound_events, log("soundevents_generated"), loop_event_names, _ranges, _vols, _levels)
    if GENERATE_STEAM_PARTICLES:
        steam_log = ["# env_steam -> info_particle_system. Replace each entity with an info_particle_system at the same "
                     "origin/angles: effect_name = the particle below, start_active = 1 for InitialState 1.",
                     "# Source1 emits along the entity's forward axis (the direction column below). Give the info_particle_system the same angles; "
                     f"the particle sends the jet along its local {STEAM_EMIT_AXIS.upper()} axis (STEAM_EMIT_AXIS)."]
        built = steam_built
        if STEAM_FROM_VMAP:
            ents, notes_s = find_env_steam(vmaps)
            steam_log += notes_s
            steam_log.append("# vmap\tclass targetname\torigin\tangles\tSource1 jet direction\tcurrent effect_name\t-> effect_name to use\tstart_active")
            for _vm, _tn, _org, _ang, _kv, _cls, _eff in ents:
                _nm = steam_particle_name(_kv)
                if _nm not in built:
                    built[_nm] = make_steam_particle(export_dir, _nm, _kv)
                    generated_particles.extend(built[_nm][2] if built[_nm][0] else [f"{_nm}\t{_steam_status(built[_nm][1])}"])
                _want = f"particles/steam/{_nm}.vpcf"
                if not built[_nm][0]:
                    _todo = _steam_status(built[_nm][1])
                elif _cls != "info_particle_system":
                    _todo = f"{_want}   (replace this {_cls} with an info_particle_system)"
                elif _eff.lower() == _want:
                    _todo = "OK, already uses it"
                else:
                    _todo = f"{_want}   (CHANGE effect_name)"
                steam_log.append(f"{_vm}\t{_cls} {_tn or '(unnamed)'}\torigin {_org}\tangles {_ang}\t"
                                 f"{_angles_forward(_ang)}\tnow: {_eff or '-'}\t-> {_todo}\tstart_active="
                                 f"{'1' if _steam_str(_kv, 'InitialState', '0').strip() == '1' else '0'}")
            if not ents and not notes_s:
                steam_log.append("# no env_steam entities found in the .vmap files")
        for _nm, _kv in STEAM_EFFECTS.items():
            ok_s, msg_s, ln_s = make_steam_particle(export_dir, _nm, _kv)
            generated_particles.extend(ln_s if ok_s else [f"{_nm}\t{_steam_status(msg_s)}"])
            steam_log.append(f"(STEAM_EFFECTS)\t{_nm}\t" + ("effect_name=particles/steam/" + _nm + ".vpcf" if ok_s else _steam_status(msg_s)))
        write_log("env_steam", steam_log)
    write_log("generated_particles", sorted(generated_particles))
    if FIX_SOUND_ENTITIES and sound_events:
        _sn, _sl = fix_sound_entities(vmaps, sound_events, export_dir)
        write_log("sound_entities", _sl)
        print(f"  sound entities: {_sn} sound path(s) replaced by soundevent names  (details: {os.path.basename(log('sound_entities'))})")
    Path(log("sound_entity_check")).write_text(
        "\n".join(check_sound_entities(vmaps, sound_events, export_dir)), encoding="utf-8")
    if RUN.stub_cs2_vmats:
        Path(log("cs2_stub_materials")).write_text(
            "# CS2 ships these vmats with the error shader and no textures; they were re-ported from Source1 where possible\n"
            + "\n".join(sorted(RUN.stub_cs2_vmats)), encoding="utf-8")
    rename_plus_refs(vmaps, BACKUP_DIR)
    if CONVERT_FIRE_SPARKS:
        _fs = convert_fire_and_sparks(vmaps, export_dir)
        step("fire_sparks", _fs, tail(_fs, "fire / sparks") + " ported")
    if CONVERT_STEAM_TRAILS:
        _st = convert_steam_and_trails(vmaps, export_dir)
        step("steam_trails", _st, tail(_st, "steam / sprite trails") + " converted")
    if DUSTMOTES_PARTICLES:
        per_vmf("dustmotes", lambda g, v: convert_dustmotes(g, v, export_dir), _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# func_dustmotes") and ": 0 converted" not in ls[0] else "")
    if DOOR_UNBREAKABLE:
        step("door_unbreakable", add_door_unbreakable(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if ROTDOOR_ONE_WAY:
        step("rotdoor_direction", fix_rotdoor_direction(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if LOGIC_CASE_NUMERIC_FIX or LOGIC_CASE_FLOAT_TEXT:
        step("counter_cases", fix_counter_cases(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if ADDOUTPUT_OUTPUTS_GATED:        # first: the outputs it makes static are converted by every pass after it (equips, names, speedmod ...)
        _ag = gate_addoutput_outputs(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("addoutput_outputs", _ag, _ag[0][2:] if len(_ag) > 1 else "")
    if ADDOUTPUT_FIX:
        step("addoutput", convert_addoutputs(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if LASERS_TESLAS:
        if SPOTLIGHTS:
            per_vmf("spotlights", convert_spotlights, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
        _LASER_VMF_OF.clear()
        _LASER_VMF_OF.update(vmf_of)
        step("lasers_teslas", convert_lasers_and_teslas(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir))
    if PARTICLE_PORT:
        step("particles", convert_particle_systems(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir))
    if HIDDEN_FACE_FIX:
        per_vmf("hidden_faces", fix_hidden_faces, vmaps, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
    if FACE_SCALE_FIX:
        def _face_scales(group, vmf):
            _FACE_SCALES_PATCHED.clear()
            lines = fix_face_scales(group, vmf, in_place=True)
            # a second pass only finds something after the first one patched faces (it can then tell which brush they are): skip it
            # when nothing was patched (each pass re-reads the map and the .vmf: ~10 s on mg_hellz)
            if vmf and any(_FACE_SCALES_PATCHED.values()):
                _face_scales_settle(group, vmf, "on a second pass (faces the first pass made identifiable)")
            return lines
        per_vmf("face_scale_fix", _face_scales, vmaps, need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: "")
        if SKEWED_AXIS_FIX:
            per_vmf("skewed_axes", fix_skewed_texture_axes, vmaps, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
        if BROKEN_SCALE_BY_PLANE:
            per_vmf("broken_scales", fix_broken_scales_by_plane, vmaps, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
        per_vmf("absurd_scales", report_absurd_scale_faces, vmaps, need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: "face scales: " + ls[0][2:].split(": ")[0] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") and "still have" in ls[0] else "")
        if _no_vmf:
            print("  [NOTE] face scales: no .vmf of the same name for " + ", ".join(os.path.basename(str(v)) for v in _no_vmf[:4])
                  + ", so wrong texture SCALES cannot be fixed there (set STATIC_OVERLAY_VMF); texture coordinates were still checked")
    # after the face scales: that step puts back the .vmf's mapping (on a first run it differs from the importer's in scale too), so a patch
    # turned before it was turned back on every first run. Turned after it, the face-scale step recognises the turn on later runs and keeps it
    if MIRRORED_TEXTURE_FIX:
        _mt = fix_mirrored_textures(vmaps, export_dir)
        step("mirrored_textures", _mt, tail(_mt, "mirrored textures"))
    if SHARED_PARENT_FIX:
        per_vmf("shared_parents", fix_shared_parent_names, _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") and not ls[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if BRUSH_IO_REVIEW:
        per_vmf("brush_io_review", report_brush_io, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:].split(", to check")[0] + ": " + ls[0].rsplit(": ", 1)[-1] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") and not ls[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if REFRACT_FACES_NODRAW and REFRACT_FACES:
        per_vmf("refract_faces", hide_refract_faces, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") and ": 0 mesh" not in ls[0] else "")
    if ANIM_SHEET_TILE_CUT:       # after the face scales and mirrored textures, which set the faces' texture coordinates
        per_vmf("anim_tiles", cut_animated_sheet_tiles, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") and not ls[0].startswith("# animated-sheet faces cut per texture tile: 0 ") else "")
    if DISP_REBUILD:       # after the face scale fix (it no longer has the importer's displacement tables to correct)
        per_vmf("displacements", rebuild_displacements, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: tail(ls, "displacements"))
    _ov_lines = static_overlay_report(vmaps, export_dir)
    _ov_parts = []
    for _vmf, _group in group_by_vmf(vmaps, vmf_of):
        print(f"  static overlays: using {_vmf} for the surface directions")
        _fix = fix_static_overlays(_group, _vmf, in_place=STATIC_OVERLAY_PATCH_IN_PLACE)
        _ov_parts.append((_vmf, _fix))
        _kinds = collections.Counter(_l.split("\t")[0].split(" (")[0] for _l in _fix if not _l.startswith("#"))
        print("  static overlays: " + ", ".join(f"{_n} {_k}" for _k, _n in sorted(_kinds.items())) +
              ("" if STATIC_OVERLAY_PATCH_IN_PLACE else
               "  -- nothing was written to the vmap: STATIC_OVERLAY_PATCH_IN_PLACE is False"))
    if _ov_parts:
        write_log("static_overlay_fix", (_l for _vmf, _fix in _ov_parts for _l in _fix))
        # with a .vmf the per-overlay lines above (all PLACEHOLDER, all identical values) carry nothing the fix lines do not: keep a material summary + the fix table
        _mat_where = {}
        for _ln in _ov_lines:
            _c = _ln.split("\t")
            if len(_c) > 4 and not _ln.startswith("#"):
                _mat_where.setdefault((_c[3], _c[4]), 0)
                _mat_where[(_c[3], _c[4])] += 1
        _head = [_ov_lines[0], "# Materials used by the overlays (count, where the vmat is):"]
        _head += [f"#   {_n}x  {_m}  [{_w}]" for (_m, _w), _n in sorted(_mat_where.items())]
        _head += ["# Set each overlay below to the right-hand values (the '*' ones differ). Origin is the overlay's own origin; Angles are pitch yaw roll; "
                  "size = quad corners; keep Scale 1 1 1. Rerun to check: fixed ones turn OK.", ""]
        if _no_vmf:
            _head.insert(1, "# NO ANGLES for the overlays of " + ", ".join(os.path.basename(str(v)) for v in _no_vmf)
                         + ": no .vmf of the same name (the vmap alone does not hold them). Set STATIC_OVERLAY_VMF to the decompiled .vmf and rerun.")
        _ov_lines = list(_head)
        for _vmf, _fix in _ov_parts:
            if len(_ov_parts) > 1:
                _ov_lines.append(f"# ===== .vmf: {_vmf}")
            _ov_lines += [_fix[0]] + sorted(_fix[1:], key=lambda _l: (_l.split("\t")[1] if "\t" in _l else "", _l))
    else:
        _ov_lines.insert(1, "# NO ANGLES/ORIENTATION BELOW: the vmap does not contain them, and no .vmf of the map's name was found under SOURCE1_ROOTS/maps. "
                            "Set STATIC_OVERLAY_VMF (top of the script) to the decompiled .vmf and rerun.")
        print("  [NOTE] static overlays: set STATIC_OVERLAY_VMF to list the angles each overlay needs (the vmap alone cannot tell)")
    write_log("static_overlays", _ov_lines)
    if OVERLAY_ENTITY_QUADS:
        _oq = convert_entity_overlays(vmaps, export_dir)
        step("overlay_entity_quads", _oq, "overlay quads: " + _oq[0][2:])
    if STATIC_OVERLAY_FIT_DEPTH:
        _od = fit_overlay_depths(vmaps, vmf_of)
        step("overlay_depths", _od, _od[0][2:])
    if WEAPON_PROP_SWAP:
        step("weapon_props", swap_weapon_props(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), BACKUP_DIR, vmf_of))
    if PROPDATA_MISSING_MODELS:
        step("propdata_props", fix_propdata_props(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if True:                          # (also with FUNC_CLIP_VPHYSICS_PUSHAWAY off: turns back what an earlier run changed) before the mass rename, which renames the prop_physics_override it makes (PHYSBOX_PROPS makes them so itself)
        _cp = clip_vphysics_pushaway(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("clip_vphysics_pushaway", _cp, _cp[0][2:] if len(_cp) > 1 else "")
    if PROP_MASS_RENAME:
        _pm = rename_props_by_mass(vmaps, BACKUP_DIR, in_place=PROP_MASS_IN_PLACE)
        step("prop_mass_rename", _pm, "prop masses: " + (_pm[0][2:] if _pm else "none"))
    if PHYSBOX_SET_MASS:                 # after the rename: the SetMass goes to the physbox's final name, with the mass the name carries
        _sm = set_physbox_masses(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("physbox_mass", _sm, _sm[0][2:] if _sm else "")
    if PHYSBOX_MULTIPLAYER_TO_PROP:     # after the masses (worked out from the brushwork it replaces)
        _pp = physbox_multiplayer_to_props(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir)
        step("physbox_props", _pp, _pp[0][2:] if _pp and not _pp[0].split(":")[1].startswith(" 0,") else "")
    if PHYS_TRIGGER_WAKE:                # after the rename (the Wake goes to the object's final name)
        _pw = wake_physics_in_triggers(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("physics_wake", _pw, _pw[0][2:] if _pw and not _pw[0].endswith(": 0 output(s) added") else "")
    if TRIGGER_MATERIAL_FIX:
        _tm = fix_trigger_materials(vmaps)
        step("trigger_materials", _tm, tail(_tm, "triggers"))
    if HEAL_TRIGGER_REPORT and not (MAP_SCRIPTS and HEAL_TRIGGERS_TO_SCRIPT):     # (with them on, the map scripts step turns them into heal zones)
        _ht = report_heal_triggers(vmaps)
        step("heal_triggers", _ht, "[NOTE] heal triggers: " + _ht[0][2:] if _ht[0].split(": ")[-1] != "0" else "")
    if NULL_PARAM_FIX:
        _np = fix_null_params(vmaps)
        step("null_params", _np, tail(_np, "null params"))
    if OBSOLETE_ENTITIES:
        step("obsolete_entities", fix_obsolete_entities(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if EQUIP_CHECK:
        _eq = check_player_equips(vmaps)
        step("player_equips", _eq, "equips: " + _eq[0][2:].split(". ")[0].replace("game_player_equip: ", ""))
    if BRUSH_RENDER_FIX:
        _br = fix_brush_render(vmaps, BACKUP_DIR)
        step("brush_render", _br, "brushes: " + _br[0][2:].split(". ")[0])
    if RENDERMODE_CS2:
        per_vmf("cs2_keyvalues", lambda g, v: fix_cs2_keyvalues(g, v), vmaps, need_vmf=False)
    if ROPE_SLACK:
        per_vmf("rope_slack", set_rope_slack, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and not ls[0].endswith(": 0 rope(s) set") else "")
    if ROPE_MATERIALS:
        _rm = convert_rope_materials(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir)
        step("rope_materials", _rm, _rm[0][2:] if _rm else "")
    if ROPE_CLIENTSIDE:
        per_vmf("particle_ropes", convert_particle_ropes, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# path_particle_rope") and not ls[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if SHARED_NAME_WILDCARD:
        per_vmf("shared_targets", wildcard_shared_targets, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# outputs to a name") and not ls[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if AMBIGUOUS_PARENT_FIX:
        per_vmf("ambiguous_parents", fix_ambiguous_parents, _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# parent names") and not ls[0].startswith("# parent names several entities share: 0 ") else "")
    if SHARED_NAME_REPORT:
        per_vmf("shared_names", report_shared_names, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: "")
    if FUNC_BRUSH_REVIEW:
        per_vmf("func_brush_review", report_switched_brushes, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: "")
    if WATER_VOLUMES:
        _wmt = {v: _vmap_version(v) for v in vmaps if os.path.isfile(v)}
        _wv = per_vmf("water", lambda g, v: add_water_volumes(g, export_dir, BACKUP_DIR, v), vmaps, need_vmf=False,
                      head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:].split(". ")[0] if ls else "water: none")
        for _m in [x.split("\t")[1] for x in _wv if x.startswith("MATERIAL\t") and x.split("\t")[2] == "MISSING"]:
            print(f"  [MISSING] water material {_m}: CS2 has no such material; give that water a CS2 water material in Hammer")
        _wch = [v for v in vmaps if os.path.isfile(v) and _vmap_version(v) != _wmt.get(v)]     # only maps the water pass changed
        if FACE_SCALE_FIX:
            for _vmf, _group in group_by_vmf(_wch, vmf_of):
                _face_scales_settle(_group, _vmf, "on the meshes the water pass added")
    if ENTITY_PLAYERCLIP_LAYER:
        _ep = entity_playerclip_layer(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("entity_playerclip", _ep, _ep[0][2:] if len(_ep) > 1 else "")
    if WATER_BUOYANCY and WATER_VOLUMES:     # after the water pass: the func_waters and their depth boxes exist by then
        _wbt = {v: _vmap_version(v) for v in vmaps if os.path.isfile(v)}
        _wb = water_buoyancy(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("water_buoyancy", _wb, _wb[0][2:] if len(_wb) > 1 else "")
        _wbc = [v for v in vmaps if os.path.isfile(v) and _vmap_version(v) != _wbt.get(v)]
        if FACE_SCALE_FIX and _wbc:        # the trigger's copied faces, as the face-scale steps of a rerun would leave them
            import io as _io_wb, contextlib as _cl_wb
            for _vmf, _group in group_by_vmf(_wbc, vmf_of):
                if _face_scales_settle(_group, _vmf, "on the trigger_buoyancy faces"):
                    # the settle runs over the whole map: the face-scale block's follow-ups again, so the faces they fixed are as a rerun leaves them
                    with _cl_wb.redirect_stdout(_io_wb.StringIO()):
                        if SKEWED_AXIS_FIX and _vmf:
                            fix_skewed_texture_axes(_group, _vmf)
                        if BROKEN_SCALE_BY_PLANE and _vmf:
                            fix_broken_scales_by_plane(_group, _vmf)
    if DECOMPILE_SCALE_FIX:        # after every face-scale step: on a fresh import those put the .vmf's rounded scale (0.0313) back on the faces
        # the importer got wrong (mg_mario_party's laser_mover: "38 faces re-scaled ... texture coordinates rewritten"), undoing it
        per_vmf("decompile_scales", fix_decompile_scales, vmaps, head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# ") else "")
    if WORLDTEXT_FIX:
        per_vmf("worldtext", fix_worldtext, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and not ls[0].endswith(": none in the .vmf") else "")
    if AREAPORTAL_FADE_BRUSH:      # before the generated compile: it writes <material>_fade<NN>.vmat
        per_vmf("areaportal_fade", lambda g, v: fix_areaportal_fade_brushes(g, v, export_dir), _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and not ls[0].endswith(": none in the .vmf") else "")
    if PHYSBOX_EXACT_HULLS:
        _ph = physbox_exact_hulls(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("physbox_hulls", _ph, _ph[0][2:] if _ph and not _ph[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if CONVEYOR_SCROLL:            # after every pass that matches faces to the .vmf by material; before the generated compile (it writes vmats)
        _cs = conveyor_scroll_materials(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir)
        step("conveyor_scroll", _cs, _cs[0][2:] if _cs and not _cs[0].startswith("# func_conveyor scrolling faces: 0 ") else "")
    if GENERATED_COMPILE:          # after the water pass, which writes the converted water materials
        step("generated_compile", compile_generated_assets(export_dir))
    if SPAWN_FLOOR_FIX:            # after the water pass: the floors Valve's importer merged into a func_water are world again by then
        step("spawn_heights", fix_spawn_heights(_playable_vmaps(vmaps)))
    if EQUIP_SCRIPT and MAP_SCRIPTS:      # before add_map_scripts, which writes the equips into player_equip.js
        per_vmf("equips_script", convert_equips, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:])
    if CSGO_TELEPORTS and MAP_SCRIPTS:    # before add_map_scripts, which writes the triggers into teleport_cycle.js
        per_vmf("shared_teleports", convert_shared_teleports, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:])
    if SOFT_BARRIERS and MAP_SCRIPTS:     # before add_map_scripts, which writes the barriers into softbarrier.js
        per_vmf("soft_barriers", convert_soft_barriers, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:])
    if PHYS_THRUSTER_FORCE:          # after the prop renames: the mass comes from push_<kg>_ names
        _th = scale_thruster_forces(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("thruster_force", _th, _th[0][2:] if len(_th) > 1 else "")
    if FUNC_CLIP_VPHYSICS_SOLID:
        _cv = clip_vphysics_solid(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("clip_vphysics_solid", _cv, _cv[0][2:] if len(_cv) > 1 else "")
    if TRIGGER_GRAVITY_TO_SCRIPT and MAP_SCRIPTS:   # before add_map_scripts, which adds player_velocity.js and registers the Gravity_ inputs
        _tg = convert_trigger_gravity(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("trigger_gravity", _tg, _tg[0][2:] if len(_tg) > 1 else "")
    if AMBIENT_KILL_STOPS:
        per_vmf("ambient_kill_stops", lambda g, v: ambient_kill_stops(g, v), _playable_vmaps(vmaps), need_vmf=False,
                head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if len(ls) > 1 else "")
    if SCREEN_OVERLAYS and MAP_SCRIPTS:   # before add_map_scripts, which writes the overlays into screen_overlay.js
        _so = convert_screen_overlays(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir)
        step("screen_overlays", _so, _so[0][2:] if _so else "")
    _push_data, _pl = prepare_trigger_pushes(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), on=TRIGGER_PUSH_SCRIPT and MAP_SCRIPTS)
    step("trigger_push", _pl)
    if MAP_SCRIPTS:
        _ms = add_map_scripts(_playable_vmaps(vmaps), export_dir, _push_data)
        step("map_scripts", _ms, "")
        print("  " + _ms[0][2:])
    if LIGHTING_REBUILD in ("once", "always"):
        _lt = per_vmf("lighting", lambda g, v: rebuild_map_lighting(g, v, BACKUP_DIR), _main_vmaps(vmaps, primary), need_vmf=False, head=lambda ls: "")
        for _l in _lt:
            if _l.startswith("# ") and not _l.startswith("# ===== "):
                print("  lighting: " + _l[2:])
    if PROBE_COVER_ENTITIES:         # after the lighting rebuild, which makes the probe volumes
        _pc = probe_cover_entities(_main_vmaps(vmaps, primary))
        step("probe_cover", _pc, _pc[0][2:] if _pc and not _pc[0].endswith(": 0") else "")
    if LIGHT_IO_FIX:                 # after the lighting rebuild, which recreates the lights
        _li = fix_light_inputs(_playable_vmaps(vmaps))
        step("light_inputs", _li, tail(_li, "light inputs"))
    if ENTITY_SEAM_REPORT:
        _es = report_entity_seams(_main_vmaps(vmaps, primary))
        step("entity_seams", _es, "entity seams: " + _es[0][2:].split(". ")[0].replace("entity seams: ", ""))
    if RADAR:
        _rd = make_radars(vmaps, primary, export_dir, BACKUP_DIR)
        for _l in _rd:
            if _l.startswith("# ") and not _l.startswith("# radar:"):
                print("  radar: " + _l[2:])
        step("radar", _rd, f"radar: {sum(1 for _l in _rd if _l.startswith('WROTE'))} file(s) written, {sum(1 for _l in _rd if _l.startswith('UNCHANGED'))} unchanged, "
                           f"{sum(1 for _l in _rd if _l.startswith('KEPT'))} kept as you edited them (map unchanged), "
                           f"{sum(1 for _l in _rd if _l.startswith('REPLACED'))} edited file(s) redrawn because the map changed")
    if REPORT_MISSING_ENTITIES:
        per_vmf("missing_entities", report_missing_entities, _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: "\n".join("missing entities: " + _l[2:].split(";")[1].strip() for _l in ls if _l.startswith("# ") and ".vmf entities;" in _l))
    if REPORT_VSCRIPTS:
        per_vmf("vscripts", report_vscripts, _playable_vmaps(vmaps), head=lambda ls: ls[0][2:] if ls and ls[0].startswith("# VScript") else "")
    if REPORT_NEVER_ENABLED:
        per_vmf("never_enabled", report_never_enabled, _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: "\n".join(x[2:] for x in ls[:2] if x.startswith("# ") and not x.startswith("#  ")))
    if REPORT_DROPPED_IO:
        per_vmf("dropped_io", lambda g, v: report_dropped_io(g, v, restore_self=RESTORE_SELF_IO), _playable_vmaps(vmaps),
                head=lambda ls: "\n".join("dropped IO: " + _l[2:].replace("outputs dropped from matched owners", "outputs dropped")
                                            for _l in ls if _l.startswith("# ") and "owners matched" in _l))
    _DMX_DOC_RO.clear()            # (the parsed maps the three reports above shared)
    Path(log("sprites_mapped")).write_text(
        "\n".join(f"{k}\t-> {v}" for k, v in sorted(sprite_refs.items())), encoding="utf-8")
    write_log("models_imported", sorted(models_imported))
    _remap_recs = orphan_records if VMDL_REMAP_BARE_MATERIALS else \
        {r_ for r_ in orphan_records if MISSING_BLACK_FIX and r_[2] == (cs2_black_material(),)}
    _remap_recs = set(_remap_recs) | iris_recs
    if EYE_IRIS_BAKE:
        write_log("eye_iris", ["# Eyes materials with their iris baked in (EYE_IRIS_BAKE): "
                               f"{sum(1 for _l in iris_rows if _l.startswith('BAKED'))} baked"] + iris_rows)
    if _remap_recs:
        _rm = remap_bare_vmdl_materials(export_dir, _remap_recs)
        if _rm:
            step("vmdl_material_remaps", _rm, f"model materials: {sum(1 for _l in _rm if _l.startswith('REMAP'))} bare material name(s) remapped in .vmdl files")
    _bg = fix_vmdl_bodygroup_names(export_dir) if VMDL_BODYGROUP_NAMES else []
    if RAGDOLL_SHAPES_FIX:
        _rs = ragdoll_shapes_fix(export_dir)
        if _rs:
            write_log("ragdoll_shapes", _rs)
            print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _rs if _l.startswith('SHAPES'))} ragdoll model(s) given the collision the import left out")
    if RAGDOLL_DEFAULT_POSE:
        _rp = ragdoll_default_pose(export_dir)
        if _rp:
            write_log("ragdoll_pose", _rp)
            print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _rp if _l.startswith('DEFAULT'))} ragdoll model(s) given their first animation as the default pose")
    if RAGDOLL_BIND_POSE:
        _rb = ragdoll_bind_pose(export_dir)
        if _rb:
            write_log("ragdoll_bind_pose", _rb)
            print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _rb if _l.startswith('BIND_POSE'))} ragdoll model(s) given CS:GO's starting pose as their rest pose")
    if MODEL_SPHERE_HULLS:
        _sh = model_sphere_hulls(export_dir)
        if _sh:
            write_log("model_spheres", _sh)
            print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _sh if _l.startswith('SPHERE'))} round model(s) given a true sphere collision")
    if MODEL_DEFAULT_POSE:
        _dp = bake_model_default_pose(export_dir)
        _bg += _dp
        if _dp:
            print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _dp if _l.startswith('POSE_BAKED'))} model(s) with their CS:GO default pose baked into the mesh")
    if _bg:
        print(f"  models: {sum(1 for _l in _bg if _l.startswith('BODYGROUP_NAMED'))} .vmdl file(s) given body group choice names")
    if COMPILE_MODELS:
        _mc = compile_models(export_dir)
        step("models_compiled", _bg + _mc[2], f"models: {_mc[0]} compiled, {_mc[1]} failed, {_mc[3]} already up to date")
    elif _bg:
        step("models_compiled", _bg, "models: body group choice names given")
    write_log("models_skipped", sorted(models_skipped))
    orphan_lines = []
    for o, model, cands in sorted(orphan_records):
        if not cands:
            orphan_lines.append(f"{o}\t(model: {model})\t-> UNRESOLVED: not in the .mdl material list, "
                                f"no VMT found in the model's folder")
            continue
        states = []
        for c in cands:
            if c in converted:
                states.append(f"{c} (converted)")
            elif c in verified_only:
                states.append(f"{c} (already in CS2)")
            elif exists_out(c):
                states.append(f"{c} (exists in addon)")
            else:
                states.append(f"{c} (NOT converted - see missing_reasons)")
        orphan_lines.append(f"{o}\t(model: {model})\t-> " + "; ".join(states))
    write_log("dmx_orphan_vmats", orphan_lines)

    _saved = _flush_vmaps()
    step("vmaps_saved", _saved, f"maps: {sum(1 for _l in _saved if _l.startswith('SAVED'))} saved"
                                + (f", {sum(1 for _l in _saved if _l.startswith('UNCHANGED'))} unchanged (rebuilt as they were: not rewritten, no backup)"
                                   if any(_l.startswith('UNCHANGED') for _l in _saved) else "")
                                + (f", {sum(1 for _l in _saved if _l.startswith('NOT_SAVED'))} could NOT be saved" if any(_l.startswith('NOT_SAVED') for _l in _saved) else ""))
    if PASS_TIMES:
        _agg = {}
        for _n, _d in _PASS_TIMES:
            _c, _s = _agg.get(_n, (0, 0.0))
            _agg[_n] = (_c + 1, _s + _d)
        _tl = [f"# total {time.time() - _t_start:.1f} s; steps by time (calls, seconds)"] + \
              [f"{_s:8.1f} s\t{_c:5d} x\t{_n}" for _n, (_c, _s) in sorted(_agg.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][1])]
        step("timings", _tl, f"timings: run {time.time() - _t_start:.0f} s; slowest: " +
             ", ".join(f"{_n} {_s:.0f} s" for _n, (_c, _s) in sorted(_agg.items(), key=lambda kv: -kv[1][1])[:5]))
    print("================================================")
    print(f"Log prefix: {log_prefix}")
    print(f"VMAPs scanned: {len(vmaps)}")
    print(f"Raw extracted strings (union): {len(all_matches)}")
    print(f"Dropped by root filter: {len(set(dropped_by_root))}")
    print(f"Valid assets found: {len(valid_assets)}")
    print(f"Processed (seen): {len(processed)}")
    print(f"Already in CS2 (skipped): {len(already_in_cs2)}")
    print(f"Converted (VMT->VMAT): {len(converted)}")
    print(f"Converted (VTF->VTEX): {len(vtex_converted)}")
    print(f"Copied (raw images / sounds): {len(copied)}")
    print(f"Models imported (cs_mdl_import): {len(models_imported)}")
    print(f"Models skipped (player models, missing .vvd/.vtx): {len(models_skipped)}")
    print(f"Models still needing conversion: {len(models_todo)}")
    print(f"Unsupported shaders (e.g. water): {len(unsupported)}")
    print(f"Missing (final, disk-checked): {len(missing_final)}")
    print(f"Failed conversions: {len(failed)}")
    print(f"Invalid filtered out: {len(invalid_assets)}")
    print("Addon folder (assets go here):", str(export_dir))
    print("Logs folder:", LOG_DIR)
    print("Backups folder:", BACKUP_DIR)
    print("================================================")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    try:
        main()
    except KeyboardInterrupt:
        _flush_vmaps()          # the maps as the passes that finished left them
        print("\n[INTERRUPTED] Importer killed. Maps changed so far are saved, and files already written stay in the addon folder; rerun to resume.")
        sys.exit(130)
    except BaseException:
        _flush_vmaps()          # a pass crashed: keep what the passes before it did (as when each pass saved its own changes)
        raise
